title: '2026-11-13, 21:10 UTC: Jeff''s bare M: his server drew the old title, and his history cannot show whether his buffer still showed it. View snapshots, now on main, would show it next time.'
pid: 44ad1797-26f2-4514-a514-01dd40d72e2c
body: |2-
  Mission: [[id:aaddcc37-f159-4b48-9110-567482db4ebb][Find from Jeff's history why a changed node stood in his diff view with nothing under it]].
  The finding, its timeline and the reproduction are in my note
  [[id:162cd3ea-3016-4454-8fda-aa76b879b563][2026-11-13: Jeff's bare M on 'health \ jbb']], under "what I know". In short: on a copy of his
  data rolled back to 20:34 UTC, the diff view numbers its headlines as his
  buffer did (the node is 4l), and draws the old title under it as 4m. Nothing
  in his saves removes it. No buffer was logged, so what Emacs showed cannot be
  known; a fold under 'health \ jbb' would explain it.
contains:
- 9b8ea017-0507-47eb-9b29-f7c285fbc635
- e098a111-aaee-4486-9b83-b126d4c9ffe5
